|>Newsgroups: comp.soft-sys.dce,comp.unix.osf.misc

|>My company is just getting into using DCE in our development effort.
|>We have just acquired DCE for OS/2 . What is the criteria to choose
|>a cell directory name ? (the internet address we have is maxm.com)
|>Any related information would also be useful.

	You should call it CELL_NAME.maxm.com where CELL_NAME is whatever
	you want to name it.  The ".maxm.com" will be useful when you
	start doing intercell comminications and advertise your cell
	via BIND (DNS).

	Our main cell name is mayflower.pilgrim.umass.edu where
	pilgrim.umass.edu is our domain.  mayflower.pilgrim.umass.edu
	is not a physical machine in our case  but there is no reason
	why it can't be either.  You may need to be careful if it is a named
	machine since your fully qualified cell name will need to point to
	the machine where your CDS server runs if you want to advertize the
	cell through BIND.

