In article <3b27kf$f9c@oe.sedat.de> bitter@inet_srv (Rainer Bittermann) writes:

>does anybody know if one can run OSF/DCE with MS/Windows ?
>Is there any possibility to run OSF/DCE on a PC ?
>Thanks in advance !

Yes, the Win32 SDK comes with all (most) you need to develop client/server
applicatoins using OSF/RPC. It comes with libraries for 16-bit and 32-bit
targets. The 16-bit libraries do NOT provide those RPC functions needed to
implement RPC servers.

If you want the full OSF/DCE functionality, you might consider DIGITAL's
DCE for Windows NT V3.5. It provides libraries only for 32-bit targets, but
supports RPC, CDS, TS and Security Service. Don't know about FTS.

Hope this helps.

Where is the kind soul out in netland, who prepares a FAQ concerning DCE
and RPC?

Greetings
Herbert



