In article <39lsjk$lrf@clam.hi.com> wright@clam.hi.com (David Wright) writes:
>The single biggest problem is errno handling.  Errno is a single,
>global variable in standard Unix.  (Granted, this was a really bad
>design decision, but we're stuck with it.)  Since DCE applications are
>multi-threaded, they need to be able to keep errno on a per-thread
>basis (so they don't trip over each other's values).

Since you're productizing DCE, you can change the DCE thread
implementation.  Record errno along with the hardware registers in your
thread context.  When you switch threads, switch errno values.

If you have kernel threads, your kernel should arrange to map errno
separately for each thread.

-Andrew Hastings
 Encina Development
 Transarc


