|> 
|> Since you're productizing DCE, you can change the DCE thread
|> implementation.  Record errno along with the hardware registers in your
|> thread context.  When you switch threads, switch errno values.

Why you would want to waste a valuable register on errno is beyond me, keeping
the thread id in a register would be sensible as you access it frequently but
errno? Errno is best kept in thread private data. By thread private I don't mean
inaccessible to other threads, just not used by them.

|> If you have kernel threads, your kernel should arrange to map errno
|> separately for each thread.

This is daft too. This means address space manipulations switching between
threads. On some architectures this can be very expensive. So much for threads
being light weight.

Simon.

