A draft is a draft is a draft.  DCE needed threads and posix wasn't
standardized yet.  Since then DCE 1.0, 1.0.1, 1.0.2, 1.0.3 and 1.1 will
have been released and there is still no posix threads standard, just four
or five different drafts.

>am facing now is getting the IDL compiler to build and work with something
>besides Ultix, HPUX, AIX or SunOS lex/yacc.

Oh yeah, ouch, sorry about that.  The IDL compiler sources depend on the
internals of your lex and yacc implementation.  OSF doesn't like it, but
it has never been high enough on our list to get it fixed -- other things
were deemed more important.  I updated my posting on this:
    The IDL compiler sources "recursively" call lex and yacc.  To do this they
    need to save and restore the lex and yacc state.  You will need to know
    something about the internals of your lex/yacc generated code.


