where the master replica of CDS and the SEcurity server reside comes
down.
Can the cut off cell continue to work as normal based on the replicas
we have there ? Could users still be added ( guess not ) and servers
still register into CDS ? This is important if the Unix server would
reboot and servers would register their interface dynamically I guess.

If servers couldn't register anymore because they need write access
to the replica, can we define servers manually and statically in the
CDS from the beginning ( avoiding them to write into CDS when they
start up ) ? After all, the only thing which is dynamic about most
servers is their endpoints, and those are better not put in CDS.

I ask this question because it is not very clear from the docs how
much autonomy a location has once cut off from the master CDS and
sercurity.

