	Ah, this is easy.  You remember the joke:

		Man:  	Doctor, it hurts when I do this...[wiggles arm]
		Doctor:	Don't do that!

	Well, the solution is the same for DCE and errno (also DCE and
	any other static or global data maintained outside of the DCE
	libraries).

	Don't mix thread-safe and non-threadsafe code.  You will need
	to rebuild libm and libX using appropriate header files so
	that you get the special definition of errno.

	Trying to maintain locks around this data will be a thankless
	chore.

	And while you're at it, don't forget that there's a LOT of
	libc functions that aren't thread-safe.  In fact, just about
	everything that returns a pointer is suspect [excluding the
	str functions...]

